# B2S Dev OS — always on

## Session opener
Read SESSION_CONTEXT.md before any work. Restate: current phase, active
carry-forwards, this task's model class. If the selected model does not match
the task's class, stop and say so.

SESSION_CONTEXT.md and committed code outrank your memory and this
conversation. If they conflict with what you believe, the repo wins.

## One task per window
Execute exactly one task per session. Do not batch. Do not "also fix while I'm
here." Do not continue into the next task.

## Never invent scope
If it is not in SCOPE.md, PARITY_MATRIX.md, MODULE_SPEC.md, or a signed OD in
DECISIONS.md, it does not exist. Flag and stop.

STOP and flag before: changing any entity in DATA_MODEL.md; changing
BrandConfig; changing the print engine or any @page rule; adding a dependency;
touching components/ui or components/shared; editing test/fixtures/golden.

## Hard rules (CI enforces — do not suppress or work around)
- No hex colour, brand string, currency code, URL, phone, or Arabic UI literal
  outside BrandConfig / i18n resources / CSS variables.
- Nothing imports localStorage, indexedDB, or the File System Access API except
  src/data/adapters/.
- No CDN script/link at runtime. Fonts and libraries are bundled.
- No window.print(), window.open for printing, or @page outside src/print/.
- Every import, preset load, and BrandConfig write is zod-validated before it
  reaches the store.
- No user-derived value reaches innerHTML or dangerouslySetInnerHTML.

If a guard blocks you, the guard is right. To change a rule, stop and flag for
an ADR.

## This is a port, not a greenfield build
Reproduce legacy behaviour exactly; improve only where a signed decision says
so. Money and quantity parity is exact — zero drift. Print parity is ±0.2 mm on
a physical printout. When legacy behaviour looks wrong, report it as a finding;
never silently correct it. Legacy .html files are read-only reference.

## Model class
Heavyweight: architecture, storage layer, print engine, migration importer,
returns/COGS/profit math, BrandConfig schema, all gates.
Standard: UI wiring, forms, tests, land tasks, CRUD on specified entities.

## Design boundary
components/ui and components/shared belong to the design surface. Compose and
wire; never restyle. Token-only styling. Gaps route back to design.

## Every session ends the same way
Update SESSION_CONTEXT.md and append to DEVELOPMENT_JOURNAL.md:
Date | Model | Phase/Task | Files | Issues | Next

## Report honestly
State deviations from the canonical prompt and why, done-when criteria you
could not meet, and carry-forwards discovered. Never put credentials in any
chat surface.

## Stack
Vite · React · TypeScript · zod · IndexedDB via adapter · static on Vercel.
NOT used: Next.js, SSR, any backend, any database (until P10), runtime CDN,
CSS frameworks outside the token system, localStorage as a primary store.
